{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/310051-how-to-deal-with-lucky-break","id":310051,"title":"How to deal with Lucky Break","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-12T05:29:37-08:00","id":310051,"title":"How to deal with Lucky Break","content":"I am just wondering how to run this in my game. It is a nice way to for player to keep the story going when they might not have the skill to get the job done or shit hits the fan.<br /> Now it has an aspect of &quot;be careful of what you wish for&quot; as in the example of a car crashing infront of you when all you wanted was informaton from the person's computer.<br /> <br /> It remind me in a short mage game that when the fate mage crit on a fate spell to give a person a reason to come down stairs. He did some well that the person was going to go down the stairs NOW so he fell down the stair as that was the fastest way to get there.<br /> <br /> This is not so much about gamer balance but storytelling balance.<br /> The first issuse is that misfortune that can happen when they use the power. Now it is a powerful embed and it is not something you should throw around all the time even if we forget about the chance of breaking cover. You are askign fate for something and letting it sort out how it happens. Only the end result is in the demon's hands and there can be a lot of middle that happens.<br /> <br /> What I am asking is how to deal with bad side effects as a gm. I am not one to punish players but I like to run to world fairly too. How offtend and how bad should it get?<br /> <br /> I am of the mind that the bigger think the player asks for the more likely that something bad can happen. Not saying it should happen everytime but for the player to weight to pros and cons when they use the power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second thing is scope. I know the embed could do a lot of things but where would you draw the line, What can't it do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T20:55:05-08:00","id":312732,"title":"","content":"I suggest putting a limitation on Lucky Break similar to the mechanic used for In My Pocket. The alternative is simply making use so punishingly unpredictable that people NEVER use it which is not as much fun but hey might also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T05:35:59-08:00","id":312880,"title":"","content":"I'd discuss it with the players. Bring up potentially bigger rewards for more risk of bad stuff, and see where their sweet spot is. They may prefer less amazing at lower risk, or more amazing at higher risk, but the consensus should suggest your course of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"ht